# 7. Models from files

This example shows models read from files: a camel (a single OBJ file, without texture) and the atrium of
Sponza (an OBJ file, its materials and 14 textures). The buttons of the slide choose the model, and the slide
displays its number of triangles. The point of the example is the files: how a demo for the web reads them,
and what it costs.

