## What is new

- **Files read as on the desktop:** the program reads `project::path + "assets/camel.obj"`. For the web, the
  `CMakeLists.txt` of CGP packs the folder `assets/` into `project.data` (`--preload-file`), a file next to
  `project.js` that the page downloads before the program starts.
- **The size of the demo:** `project.data` is about 4 MB here, downloaded at the first display of the slide. The
  files of Sponza were reduced for the web (coordinates rounded, images of 512 pixels at most).
- **The names of the files:** the file system of the browser is case-sensitive, as on Linux. The names written in
  `sponza.mtl` must be exactly those of the image files.
- **The model chosen by the slide:** a choice `slide::param("model", ...)` whose `on_change` places the camera for
  each model; the number of triangles is a readout (as in [example 6](../../01_tutorial/07_readout/index.html)).

